On the right is your Workspace. It looks just like a standard text message app. You simply type what you are looking for in plain English—like 'Create a search for customers with open sales orders'—hit the 'Build Search' button, and the bot goes to work."

[Scene 3: The Process Flow (How it Works)]
Visual: Show an animation of typing a request, or use a simple graphic showing arrows moving from the user's text to a database, then to an AI brain.
Audio: "So, what happens behind the scenes when you hit send? It’s a step-by-step process:

Understanding the Request: First, the system takes your plain text and turns it into a mathematical fingerprint.

Finding Examples: It uses this fingerprint to search a custom library of past saved searches. It finds the best, most relevant examples to use as a guide.

Locating Custom Fields: At the same time, the AI scans your sentence for any specific custom fields you might have mentioned. It automatically looks up the exact database IDs for those fields so the final search is perfectly customized to your system.

Writing the Code: Finally, it bundles your request, the past examples, and the custom field IDs, and hands them to the NetSuite AI. The AI then writes the exact JSON code needed to build your search."

[Scene 4: Autonomous Flow & Accuracy]
Visual: Show the bot displaying the "Thinking, configuring search, and validating..." message, followed by the final success message with the green badge and copy/view buttons.
Audio: "But here is the best part: the bot is completely autonomous and self-correcting, making it highly accurate.

When the AI writes the code, it doesn't just hand it to you and hope it works. It actively tries to save the search directly into NetSuite. If NetSuite rejects it and throws an error, the bot catches that error. It reads what went wrong, goes back to the AI, and asks it to fix the mistake. It will try to heal itself up to three times before giving up.

Plus, it has built-in guardrails. If someone tries to chat with the bot about the weather or something unrelated, it recognizes that it's out of bounds and politely asks the user to stick to NetSuite topics.

When it's done, you get a success message with the new Search ID, the code, and a button to view your brand-new saved search immediately."

